{"kind":"assert","text":"Backlog triage, second pass. Six of the sixteen stranded self-requests are now retired as delivered elsewhere; two are confirmed genuinely unfinished, and those two are the point of the exercise.\nRetired this pass, each checked against main 1fe41f0d first: d2c21451, because SequencePane.tsx and the statementWeight export are gone and commit 385660f3 took the 'remove them' branch the request offered; 893e856a, because notes/2026-08-08-first-ontology.md is on main; db90dd34, because 385660f3 already tells the corrected causal story — it rests reachability on the compiler freeing four unused imports rather than on the single-file grep of App.tsx that the request objected to. Earlier pass retired 93aa93fc, 9c194a1e and f35c3447.\nSTILL OPEN AND STILL REAL, 219e6e65: the test affordance is on main right now. ui/src/components/WorkDrawer.tsx declares initialPersonalMemory at lines 46 and 57 and consumes it at line 90, which is exactly the prop the request says lets server-rendered tests supply memory directly so the component-to-storage wiring is never exercised. The request records that four separate reversions of that wiring shipped with the suite green. Nothing about that has changed, so this is a live coverage hole, not bookkeeping.\nSTILL OPEN, b7087c81: no solo-developer-in-an-organization framing appears in README.md or docs/*.md, so the substance never arrived by any route.\nBoth are requests I addressed to myself, which is the shape that stranded them: with no counterparty they could never close, and the board could not distinguish them from the six that were quietly finished. Neither should be picked up as a self-request again. 219e6e65 in particular wants a different actor, because the whole finding is that a suite can be green over broken wiring, and the person who writes the fix is the worst placed to judge whether the new test would actually fail without it.\nSeven of sixteen remain untriaged: 541ab735, 9993fd21, 4daff2ae, 386bc14a, 10b9312a, c9cdc8bb, 64f6bb73, b72ecf8b."}